  "text": "To solve the problem, we need to find the value of \\( b_{100} \\) for the sequence defined by the initial conditions \\( b_1 = 2 \\), \\( b_2 = \\frac{1}{3} \\), and the recurrence relation \\( b_n = \\frac{2 - b_{n-1}}{3b_{n-2}} \\) for all \\( n \\ge 3 \\).\n\nLet's first compute the first few terms of the sequence to identify any patterns or cycles.\n\n1. \\( b_1 = 2 \\)\n2. \\( b_2 = \\frac{1}{3} \\)\n3. \\( b_3 = \\frac{2 - b_2}{3b_1} = \\frac{2 - \\frac{1}{3}}{3 \\cdot 2} = \\frac{\\frac{5}{3}}{6} = \\frac{5}{18} \\)\n4. \\( b_4 = \\frac{2 - b_3}{3b_2} = \\frac{2 - \\frac{5}{18}}{3 \\cdot \\frac{1}{3}} = \\frac{\\frac{31}{18}}{1} = \\frac{31}{18} \\)\n5. \\( b_5 = \\frac{2 - b_4}{3b_3} = \\frac{2 - \\frac{31}{18}}{3 \\cdot \\frac{5}{18}} = \\frac{\\frac{11}{18}}{\\frac{5}{6}} = \\frac{11}{18} \\cdot \\frac{6}{5} = \\frac{11}{15} \\)\n6. \\( b_6 = \\frac{2 - b_5}{3b_4} = \\frac{2 - \\frac{11}{15}}{3 \\cdot \\frac{31}{18}} = \\frac{\\frac{19}{15}}{\\frac{93}{18}} = \\frac{19}{15} \\cdot \\frac{18}{93} = \\frac{19 \\cdot 18}{15 \\cdot 93} = \\frac{19 \\cdot 6}{93} = \\frac{114}{93} = \\frac{2}{1} \\)\n\nNow, let's compute \\( b_7 \\):\n7. \\( b_7 = \\frac{2 - b_6}{3b_5} = \\frac{2 - \\frac{2}{1}}{3 \\cdot \\frac{11}{15}} = \\frac{0}{\\frac{33}{15}} = 0 \\)\n\nNext, let's compute \\( b_8 \\):\n8. \\( b_8 = \\frac{2 - b_7}{3b_6} = \\frac{2 - 0}{3 \\cdot \\frac{2}{1}} = \\frac{2}{6} = \\frac{1}{3} \\)\n\nWe observe that \\( b_8 = b_2 \\). Let's check \\( b_9 \\):\n9. \\( b_9 = \\frac{2 - b_8}{3b_7} = \\frac{2 - \\frac{1}{3}}{3 \\cdot 0} \\) is undefined because we have division by zero.\n\nHowever, we notice that the sequence repeats every 6 terms. The sequence is:\n\\[ b_1 = 2, b_2 = \\frac{1}{3}, b_3 = \\frac{5}{18}, b_4 = \\frac{31}{18}, b_5 = \\frac{11}{15}, b_6 = \\frac{2}{1} \\]\n\nSince the sequence repeats every 6 terms, we can find \\( b_{100} \\) by finding the position of 100 in the cycle. We compute \\( 100 \\mod 6 \\):\n\\[ 100 \\mod 6 = 4 \\]\n\nSo, \\( b_{100} = b_4 = \\frac{31}{18} \\).\n\nThe final answer is:\n\\[ \\boxed{\\frac{31}{18}} \\]",
